# Liegestuhl (M6, D-095): the stomped Kurgast lying in his deck chair, a
# one-way platform. A wooden deck chair O/l with a striped canvas sun hood
# R/w: the hood's top is ONE flat line over the middle 16 px (sprite row 0 =
# its k outline, columns 4-19 = the 16x16 hitbox), the canvas back's top,
# with his raised knees tucked right under it (D-038: drawn = the surface).
# Under the hood: grey hair, shut eyes and moustache, the white bathrobe w/i,
# his straw hat Y/o resting on his belly, pale shins c and R slippers poking
# out past the front. X legs O/l.
# idle: he breathes (frame 1: the hat on his belly rises 1 px) and a w "z"
# with a k outline rises beside his head (left margin, outside the 16 px).
# wake (telegraph): eyes open, a yawn, both arms stretched out past the
# hood's ends (frame 0 sideways, frame 1 up and out); the top stays flat.
# Faces right (head left, feet right); mirror = auto. Built with a scratch
# script (painted interior + automatic k outline), frozen to text here.
sprite = liegestuhl
size   = 24x16
origin = 12,16
hitbox = 4,0,16,16
mirror = auto
anim   = idle frames=2 ticks=30 loop
anim   = wake frames=2 ticks=10 loop
